// CONSTRUCTION SUPPLIES, the sawmill operator's counter in the timber yard north-east of Varrock.
//
// The stock is the OSRS shop's, item for item: a saw, a bolt of cloth, and bronze, iron and steel
// nails, a thousand of each. Nothing else - no hammer, which OSRS does not stock here either and
// which this build cannot stock anyway, because the hammer obj carries no cost and a shop prices
// everything off that; it would be given away. The sawmill still sells one in dialogue.
//
// WHY THIS SHOP EXISTS AT ALL. Steel nails had no source in the game but a smithing anvil at level
// 34, and Dragon Slayer asks for thirty of them to plank the Lady Lumbridge. A player under 34
// Smithing could not finish the quest without another player, on a world with no Grand Exchange.
//
// THE SAW RESTOCKS IN TEN TICKS and everything else in a hundred. That is the wiki's own split -
// it calls the saw the fastest-restocking item in the shop at about six seconds, against a minute
// or so for the rest.
//
// allstock=no: it buys back its own five lines and nothing else, so a bronze dagger cannot be
// turned into coins at a timber yard.
[construction_supplies]
scope=shared
size=8
restock=yes
stackall=yes
allstock=no
stock1=saw,1000,10
stock2=bolt_of_cloth,1000,100
stock3=nails_bronze,1000,100
stock4=nails_iron,1000,100
stock5=nails,1000,100
